The isValidCreditCard() method removes any whitespace characters from the input string using the replaceAll() method. It then applies the Luhn algorithm for credit card number validation. The algorithm involves iterating over the digits of the credit card number from right to left, doubling every second digit, and adding the resulting digits together. If the sum is divisible by 10, then the credit card number is valid.

The program outputs "Valid credit card number" or "Invalid credit card number" based on the result of the isValidCreditCard() method. The program closes the scanner object and terminates.

