```
public static string ReverseSentence(string input)
{
    // Split the input string into individual words (removing any extra spaces)
    string[] words = input.Split(new char[] {' '}, StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries);

    // Reverse the order of the words
    Array.Reverse(words);

    // Capitalize the first letter of the first word in the reversed sentence
    words[0] = char.ToUpper(words[0][0]) + words[0].Substring(1);

    // Combine the words back into a single string with spaces between them
    string output = string.Join(" ", words);

    return output;
}
```

To use this function, simply call it with a string argument representing the sentence you want to reverse:

```
string input = "the quick brown fox jumps  over the lazy   dog";
string output = ReverseSentence(input);
Console.WriteLine(output);  // "Dog lazy the over jumps fox brown quick The"
