Here is an example JavaScript function to convert a binary number to a decimal number:

```
function binaryToDecimal(binary) {
  const binaryString = String(binary);
  let decimal = 0;
  let power = 0;
  for (let I = binaryString.length - 1; I >= 0; i--) {
    const digit = parseInt(binaryString[i], 10);
    decimal += digit * Math.pow(2, power);
    power++;
  }
  return decimal;
}
```

This function takes in a binary number as a parameter and returns the equivalent decimal number. It works by converting the binary number to a string and then iterating through each digit from right to left. For each digit, it multiplies it by 2 to the power of its position (starting at 0 for the rightmost digit) and adds it to the decimal sum. Finally, the function returns the decimal sum.

